    "construction and reviewed operation wrapping perform no credential, connection or SQL I/O",
    "unreviewed execution context, actor population, pool and timeout bounds fail before I/O",
    "writer role, operation case, action and active AbortSignal are mandatory",
    "accessor-based role or database configuration is rejected without invoking getters",
    "legitimate public fixture prepares seats and restores exact memberships, versions and unused invitations",
    "admissions invitation winner restores observed cap 3 to original 4",
    "admissions activation winner restores observed cap 2 and occupied 2 to original 4",
    "successive seats and admissions cases preserve original identity and revoke only acknowledged returned invitations",
    "arbitrary SQL, foreign tenant, foreign actor and unauthorized seat values never reach PostgreSQL",
    "foreign membership identity, stale version and reordered cap update fail with no committed effect",
    "server baseline, assignment or original seat drift is rejected before any fixture DML",
    "restoration requires its committed case and rejects foreign subscription or unsupported outcomes",
    "unproved admissions cap 2 with an admitted member fails before restoration DML",
    "restoration cannot COMMIT without fresh final subscription, memberships and assignment readback",
    "only durable acknowledged intent/confirmed invitation pairs with exact reviewed actor and scope are adopted",
    "arbitrary invitation IDs and billing-actor/email changes fail before revocation SQL",
    "uncertain invitation acknowledgement adopts no result and blocks further fixture mutations",
    "confirmed invitation observations reject raw tokens and unverified original-record claims",
    "TLS chain and hostname verification destroy unverified leases; target/URI overrides are rejected",
    "abort while BEGIN is pending destroys the lease and never commits or recycles an open transaction",
    "abort during pending pool acquisition returns promptly and destroys the later lease",
    "abort while the real preparation journal waits for COMMIT intent destroys staged writes",
    "uncertain COMMIT has no automatic replay or restoration and exposes only a fixed code",
    "query timeout, private callback error and target drift are bounded and sanitized",
    "close destroys a still-open fixture transaction and blocks new connections",
    "per-operation cancellation leaves another independently acquired writer connection usable",
    "closing during acquisition cancels the wait and destroys a late lease without aborting the owner signal",
    "bounded pool preserves distinct acquired backend identities with queued clients"
  ],
